WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:16.641
This is the new president
and vice president of the Philippines

00:00:16.641 --> 00:00:20.895
during a YouTube Q&amp;A months
before their landslide election victory.

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:30.405
Ferdinand Marcos Jr., known as "Bongbong,"

00:00:30.405 --> 00:00:32.615
shares the same name as his father,

00:00:32.615 --> 00:00:36.286
the notorious autocrat who led
a military government in the Philippines,

00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:39.164
which tortured
and killed thousands of citizens

00:00:39.164 --> 00:00:43.168
while he and his family
stole billions from the public purse.

00:00:43.168 --> 00:00:46.880
But none of that stopped Bongbong
Marcos winning this year's election.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.589
The people have

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:52.052
spoken. They have given Marcos
a resounding victory.

00:00:52.052 --> 00:00:53.928
Marcos won by a landslide.

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:57.807
He got almost 59% of the votes.

00:00:57.807 --> 00:00:59.726
This was an epic win.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.853
The days after the election

00:01:01.853 --> 00:01:06.483
friends and colleagues
from pretty much everywhere asked me,

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:09.986
"How could this happen?"

00:01:09.986 --> 00:01:11.946
Using the power of social media,

00:01:11.946 --> 00:01:16.451
Marcos, his election team
and supporters have rewritten history,

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:20.121
claiming his father's
era was a time of prosperity and strength

00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:24.375
rather than murder
and theft on an industrial scale.

00:01:24.375 --> 00:01:26.002
It's frustrating for us

00:01:26.002 --> 00:01:31.508
because all this time we have been
debunking the disinformation,

00:01:31.508 --> 00:01:35.470
the lies that helped him win
this election.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.055
Please subscribe to us.

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:37.931
While Marcos's

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.935
opponents contend online misinformation
played a key role in his victory

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.978
there's no way to prove it.

00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:48.525
Meanwhile, Marcos himself has repeatedly
denied his campaign engaged in or had

00:01:48.525 --> 00:01:53.279
any connection to social media posts
with false or misleading claims.

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:57.617
I guess for the journalists
and fact checkers in other countries

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:01.371
where this could possibly happen as
well, I wish you good luck.

00:02:13.925 --> 00:02:14.926
When the iPhone was

00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:20.140
released in 2007, just under
6% of the Philippines was on the web.

00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:22.767
But smartphones changed that.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:25.895
Now, two-thirds of the country's
110 million

00:02:25.895 --> 00:02:29.941
citizens are connected
and spend 10 hours a day online.

00:02:29.941 --> 00:02:35.280
That's more than any other country.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.367
You can just imagine how much time
we spend here on social media. 

00:02:39.367 --> 00:02:42.412
Even here,  walking on the street, you can see people

00:02:42.412 --> 00:02:45.165
looking down on their phones,
not looking on the road.

00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:50.295
And then according to the data,
we use social media to gather information,

00:02:50.295 --> 00:02:54.382
including the news,
and at the same time to connect to people.

00:02:54.382 --> 00:03:00.388
So it's really our main source
of information here in the Philippines.

00:03:00.388 --> 00:03:04.934
Filipinos spend more than four hours
a day on social media, with Facebook

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:10.523
being the most popular platform
with nearly 84 million users in 2022.

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:15.153
A survey here recently
showed that more than half of the people

00:03:15.153 --> 00:03:19.115
who said that they're using social media
as their news source

00:03:19.115 --> 00:03:20.450
find it very difficult

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:24.412
to distinguish between what's true
and what's false on social media.

00:03:24.412 --> 00:03:27.916
So you can just imagine
the extent of the problem.

00:03:29.083 --> 00:03:32.712
The 2018 Cambridge Analytica scandal
saw the data mining

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:37.508
firm questioned over its work
for Donald Trump's presidential campaign.

00:03:37.508 --> 00:03:40.553
One whistle-blower described
how questionable rule of law,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:43.056
high social media usage and corruption

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:47.227
made the Philippines the perfect place
to test the limits of online manipulation.

00:03:48.853 --> 00:03:53.191
Bongbong Marcos has been building
his online presence for over a decade.

00:03:53.191 --> 00:03:56.653
During his unsuccessful 2016
run for vice president

00:03:56.653 --> 00:03:59.405
he relied heavily on online
messaging. 

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.366
 For his 2022 campaign

00:04:01.366 --> 00:04:05.745
he sidestepped traditional media,
instead speaking directly to voters online

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.538
in short video blogs.

00:04:07.538 --> 00:04:12.418
He gets a lot of engagements for that
and a lot of people like that about him, 

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:17.924
the vlog thing, they really patronized
that because I guess it humanizes him.

00:04:20.385 --> 00:04:26.349
I've seen analysis on social media saying
that he intentionally did not attend

00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:34.232
debates and interviews because that was
what contributed to his loss in 2016.

00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:36.109
So there was

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:39.946
a revisiting of
the strategy, the campaign strategy, and

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:45.410
as we are able to see now, we could say
that it has been effective.

00:04:49.247 --> 00:04:54.794
Bongbong has over 7 million followers on
Facebook and another 2 million on YouTube.

00:04:54.794 --> 00:05:02.051
His supporters flood news feeds
and message boards with election messages.

00:05:02.051 --> 00:05:05.972
But political posts
and videos are often disguised.

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:10.226
A lot of the disinformation
that's spreading on social media,

00:05:10.226 --> 00:05:14.439
especially in the lead up to
the elections, comes in the form of news.

00:05:14.439 --> 00:05:18.651
Some are quoting personalities

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:23.114
inaccurately, but are presented
in such a way that they look like

00:05:23.114 --> 00:05:29.412
and even imitate
the colors of mainstream media.

00:05:29.412 --> 00:05:30.455
While VeraFiles,

00:05:30.455 --> 00:05:34.500
other news organizations and Marcos's
opponents cite dozens of instances

00:05:34.500 --> 00:05:36.419
of what they call disinformation,

00:05:36.419 --> 00:05:41.132
the term itself can be problematic.
In the context of political campaigns

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:46.262
messaging regularly relies on exaggeration
and half truths, often labeled as spin.

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:49.098
Inside this gray area, social

00:05:49.098 --> 00:05:54.395
media has thrived as a powerful tool
for politicians everywhere.

00:05:55.146 --> 00:05:56.856
In the well over 600 posts

00:05:56.856 --> 00:06:00.651
fact checked by VeraFiles,
a large majority attacked Marcos's rival.

00:06:01.402 --> 00:06:04.155
While positive misinformation was skewed
the other way.

00:06:04.572 --> 00:06:09.285
And a huge number of that actually benefited
Bongbong Marcos

00:06:09.285 --> 00:06:13.164
in the way that it hyped up
his presidential campaign

00:06:13.164 --> 00:06:16.959
and it also tried to distort
historical facts

00:06:16.959 --> 00:06:18.252
regarding his family.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.217
In the 1970s, Ferdinand

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:28.638
Marcos had led a military government
of uncommon brutality.

00:06:28.638 --> 00:06:32.892
He disbanded Congress, silenced the media
and used the army to torture

00:06:32.892 --> 00:06:35.645
and kill thousands of citizens.

00:06:35.645 --> 00:06:38.648
Through all of this, Marcos
and his wife, Imelda, became

00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:42.735
exceedingly wealthy
by siphoning money from state funds.

00:06:42.735 --> 00:06:47.824
All the while, the Philippines
economy crashed and many people suffered.

00:06:48.991 --> 00:06:50.993
A critical part of Bongbong Marcos's

00:06:50.993 --> 00:06:54.038
election campaign
was convincing millions of people

00:06:54.038 --> 00:06:56.082
these things simply didn't happen.

00:06:58.292 --> 00:07:02.964
Despite the brickbats, the criticism,
the pure hate

00:07:02.964 --> 00:07:07.301
that has been heaped
upon him over the last 30-plus years,

00:07:07.301 --> 00:07:11.431
his memory,
his legacy continues to endure.

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:16.144
The Ferdinand Marcos era is portrayed
by his supporters as one of prosperity,

00:07:16.144 --> 00:07:19.897
despite economic downturn.

00:07:19.897 --> 00:07:24.819
Thousands of citizens labeled enemies 
of the state were killed and tortured.

00:07:24.819 --> 00:07:27.822
Extravagant parties
on the presidential yacht...

00:07:27.822 --> 00:07:30.366
And discussions
about the billions of dollars stolen

00:07:30.366 --> 00:07:31.868
are met with blanket denials.

00:07:31.868 --> 00:07:35.705
Ferdinand Jr. is the man
in the flashing bow tie.

00:07:35.705 --> 00:07:39.375
Social media helped spread this message,
with Marcos Jr. claiming

00:07:39.375 --> 00:07:43.629
he was presenting
his own version of history.

00:07:44.255 --> 00:07:48.342
The love for the Marcoses never really left here
in the Philippines.

00:07:48.342 --> 00:07:51.262
Even after they were ousted,
they maintained

00:07:51.262 --> 00:07:55.016
quite a strong bailiwick
in the northern Philippines.

00:07:55.016 --> 00:07:58.728
And that's
where the most loyal supporters are.

00:07:59.437 --> 00:08:03.316
It's possible Marcos would have won
even if social media wasn't part

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:05.276
of the equation.

00:08:05.276 --> 00:08:09.405
His huge margin of victory could owe more
to alliances with local leaders,

00:08:09.405 --> 00:08:12.825
endorsements by parties
affiliated with former presidents

00:08:12.825 --> 00:08:14.285
and loyalty to his family

00:08:14.285 --> 00:08:18.080
among the political elite
and everyday citizens.

00:08:18.080 --> 00:08:21.125
It's hard to determine
whether online disinformation played

00:08:21.125 --> 00:08:23.878
a critical role in Marcos
becoming president.

00:08:23.878 --> 00:08:26.714
And it's even harder
to connect it to its sources,

00:08:26.714 --> 00:08:29.175
let alone anyone directing the effort.

00:08:35.806 --> 00:08:39.977
When I talked to people and asked them
who they were inclined to support,

00:08:39.977 --> 00:08:43.523
if they said Bongbong Marcos
I would say why?

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:47.902
And there would be this gauzy look
and these sentiments expressed like,

00:08:47.902 --> 00:08:49.779
you know, his father was a great man,

00:08:49.779 --> 00:08:51.322
he was a strong leader,

00:08:51.322 --> 00:08:54.450
Philippines needs strong leadership now.

00:08:54.450 --> 00:08:57.745
And you would say, OK, well,
what about this?

00:08:57.745 --> 00:09:00.498
What about that?
What about the other thing?

00:09:00.498 --> 00:09:02.667
And they would blow it off.

00:09:02.667 --> 00:09:05.628
The response would tend to be
one of two things.

00:09:05.628 --> 00:09:10.258
They would say, "oh, look,
I was a kid then, or I wasn't born then,

00:09:10.258 --> 00:09:12.134
it's nothing to me."

00:09:12.134 --> 00:09:15.304
Or they say it's fake news.

00:09:17.098 --> 00:09:21.310
Tonight, a brutal dictator's son
winning the presidential election in the

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.479
Philippines by a landslide.

00:09:23.479 --> 00:09:27.984
Bongbong Marcos has been elected
as the next president of the Philippines.

00:09:27.984 --> 00:09:33.406
And I think that's a very
telling indication as to how successful

00:09:33.406 --> 00:09:37.702
this disinformation campaign
benefiting him is.

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:40.955
God bless the Philippines.

00:09:40.955 --> 00:09:43.207
God bless our work.

00:09:45.334 --> 00:09:47.545
The days after the election,

00:09:47.545 --> 00:09:51.257
friends and colleagues asked me,
"how could this happen?"

00:09:52.633 --> 00:09:56.304
Then I began to wonder
whether the more pertinent question was

00:09:56.304 --> 00:09:59.056
what was actually going to stop it?

00:10:01.976 --> 00:10:05.813
You have supporters, real people,

00:10:05.813 --> 00:10:08.566
and then on the other hand,
you have fake accounts.

00:10:08.899 --> 00:10:12.320
And these fake accounts, plus
the real people who are spreading this,

00:10:12.528 --> 00:10:16.907
that creates an ecosystem
wherein this disinformation spreads.

00:10:17.950 --> 00:10:22.663
We're able to monitor and flag
these online disinformation content,

00:10:22.663 --> 00:10:27.627
but we really cannot pinpoint
who is the person or the persons

00:10:27.627 --> 00:10:31.631
but one thing I can tell you
is President Bongbong Marcos,

00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:34.133
he likes to disassociate himself

00:10:34.383 --> 00:10:39.055
and his team from this information
campaign that largely benefited him.

00:10:39.055 --> 00:10:43.684
In fact, he even said that he's
actually the victim of "fake news."

00:10:43.684 --> 00:10:48.689
Some people say that
history was revised online.

00:10:48.689 --> 00:10:51.233
What do you, what is your response to that?

00:10:51.233 --> 00:10:53.694
Show me.

00:10:53.694 --> 00:10:55.821
Show me where this revisionism

00:10:55.821 --> 00:10:59.992
on our part, from our side,
whatever you want, show me.

00:11:01.661 --> 00:11:05.081
Anything that we have said
we can prove.

00:11:05.081 --> 00:11:08.834
How much of a concern is disinformation
to this administration?

00:11:08.876 --> 00:11:10.920
If any illegal acts have been committed

00:11:10.920 --> 00:11:13.964
then proper venue for
that would be the courts.

00:11:13.964 --> 00:11:16.759
But no such wrongdoing has been committed.

00:11:19.804 --> 00:11:22.807
Another major factor in Marcos's landslide
victory

00:11:22.807 --> 00:11:27.144
was the effect of his running mate,
Sara Duterte, daughter of the previous

00:11:27.144 --> 00:11:31.440
president, Rodrigo Duterte, who remains
popular in parts of the Philippines.

00:11:31.440 --> 00:11:35.236
This time around, with Sara Duterte
running by his side,

00:11:35.236 --> 00:11:39.323
he was able to win those provinces
in the southern

00:11:39.323 --> 00:11:43.327
part of the country where the Dutertes hail from.

00:11:43.327 --> 00:11:47.581
And he was able to double
the number of provinces that he was able

00:11:47.581 --> 00:11:51.585
to win compared to his 2016
vice presidential race, which he lost.

00:11:52.461 --> 00:11:56.590
It's really a consolidation
of two powerful

00:11:56.590 --> 00:12:00.970
political dynasties, political families.
One hailing from the north,

00:12:00.970 --> 00:12:05.015
that's Marcos, and the other hailing
from the south, and that's Duterte.

00:12:06.016 --> 00:12:09.562
The Philippines
excels at dynastic politics.

00:12:09.937 --> 00:12:16.527
The two presidents prior to leader Rodrigo
Duterte, they were children of presidents.

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:20.781
The lower house of our Congress,
we have majority

00:12:20.781 --> 00:12:24.785
and most of our lawmakers are products
of political dynasties.

00:12:24.827 --> 00:12:25.911
There's even a belief

00:12:25.911 --> 00:12:29.999
that the good traits,
the leadership qualities of a father or

00:12:29.999 --> 00:12:33.711
a parent
is passed down to his or her child.

00:12:34.086 --> 00:12:38.299
So that's
how much political dynasties are welcomed

00:12:38.299 --> 00:12:40.509
and elected here in the Philippines.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:46.265
While Marcos and Duterte
ran on a ticket of national unity,

00:12:46.265 --> 00:12:50.853
online their supporters pushed lies and attacked
the opposition candidate, Leni Robredo.

00:12:51.979 --> 00:12:54.482
She was accused of having an affair
while her daughters

00:12:54.482 --> 00:12:57.818
were accused of sex scandals,
all of it unsubstantiated.

00:12:58.986 --> 00:13:02.656
A lot of these Facebook pages
and Facebook groups

00:13:02.656 --> 00:13:07.495
that we were able to flag spreading
disinformation and misinformation,

00:13:07.495 --> 00:13:11.665
some of them carry his name
in their account names.

00:13:11.665 --> 00:13:17.463
And we actually also observed back in 2021
that a lot of YouTube videos

00:13:17.463 --> 00:13:21.217
that are misinforming people,
what happens is

00:13:21.217 --> 00:13:26.472
the video was uploaded on YouTube and
then there are a number of Facebook pages

00:13:26.472 --> 00:13:30.518
that reuploads it on Facebook
that also reuploads it on TikTok

00:13:30.684 --> 00:13:34.021
and this suggests that there is automation

00:13:34.021 --> 00:13:38.818
or that only one person administers
or moderates these accounts.

00:13:38.818 --> 00:13:43.489
And so it also suggests that there is
an organized effort

00:13:43.489 --> 00:13:48.911
or campaign with regards
spreading mis-and-disinformation.

00:13:50.079 --> 00:13:52.039
My father built more and better

00:13:52.039 --> 00:13:56.335
roads, produced more rice
than all administrations before his.

00:13:57.002 --> 00:13:59.630
So will it be with his son.

00:14:00.381 --> 00:14:02.758
You will get no excuses from me.

00:14:04.510 --> 00:14:07.513
Now as President, Bongbong
Marcos fashions himself

00:14:07.513 --> 00:14:11.267
as a pragmatist, 
focused on quality-of-life issues. 

00:14:11.267 --> 00:14:15.145
On foreign policy, he's promised to 
grow closer relations with China

00:14:15.145 --> 00:14:18.983
even as the two countries clash over
fishing rights in the South China Sea.

00:14:19.775 --> 00:14:22.403
All the while
maintaining historic links to the USA.

00:14:23.487 --> 00:14:29.577
This idea or this feeling or this,
shall we say, opinion

00:14:29.702 --> 00:14:35.416
I have of my father, of the man, has just
been strengthened as time goes on.

00:14:35.624 --> 00:14:39.962
What's also noteworthy is Bongbong
never talked about martial law

00:14:39.962 --> 00:14:41.422
in a negative light.

00:14:41.422 --> 00:14:45.676
It's all about admiration for his father,
a promise to continue

00:14:45.676 --> 00:14:50.681
the good projects
that came out of that era.

00:14:50.681 --> 00:14:53.392
The facts of the past is not really

00:14:53.642 --> 00:14:57.271
as effective as the facts of the present
and the future.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:02.902
Maybe it's because the people
now cannot relate with what ever happened

00:15:02.902 --> 00:15:08.032
during the martial law of Marcos Sr.,
and they actually only care

00:15:08.032 --> 00:15:12.620
about what's going to happen to them now
and what's going to happen in the future.

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:19.293
And Marcos Jr. apparently was able
to present himself effectively as someone

00:15:19.293 --> 00:15:23.297
who will bring about positive change,
who will bring hope,

00:15:23.297 --> 00:15:30.179
and who will unify the country towards
a better tomorrow or a better future.

00:15:30.179 --> 00:15:33.182
If you're going to get a platform
like social media

00:15:33.182 --> 00:15:37.519
that reaches a lot of people,
you're going to create a way

00:15:37.519 --> 00:15:42.650
by which this version of history
is going to spread, and your supporters

00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:45.277
are going to spread and believe it.

00:15:45.277 --> 00:15:48.948
Imelda Marcos famously said in
one of the documentaries about her

00:15:55.788 --> 00:15:59.875
Our job as fact checkers, and not only fact
checkers, but as journalists,

00:15:59.875 --> 00:16:06.423
as amplifiers of truth, would be
more challenging in the next six years.

00:16:06.423 --> 00:16:11.178
We're preparing for it,
and hopefully we could go through it

00:16:12.388 --> 00:16:25.901
without any problem.

